### Definitions file draft

```lean
/-
Copyright (c) 2026 ...
Released under Apache 2.0 license ...
Authors: D1-perelman-ledger builder
-/
module

public import Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.Riemannian.Basic
public import Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Basic
public import Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.ContDiff.Basic
public import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Typeclasses.Finite
public import Mathlib.Analysis.Matrix.PosDef
public import Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real

/-!
# Interfaces for Perelman's monotonicity arguments
...
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

open Bundle MeasureTheory Set
open scoped Manifold ContDiff Topology ENNReal

namespace Perelman

variable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E]
  {H : Type*} [TopologicalSpace H] {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H}
  {M : Type*} [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M]

/-! ## 1. Metric families and the Ricci flow equation -/

/-- A one-parameter family of Riemannian metrics on `M` (no regularity is assumed here). -/
abbrev MetricFamily := ℝ → Bundle.RiemannianMetric (fun x : M => TangentSpace I x)
```
Wait: `abbrev MetricFamily := ...` inside a section with variables `I M` — the abbreviation will have implicit params inferred. Better to write `abbrev MetricFamily (I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H) (M : Type*) [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M] := ...`? With section variables, Lean generalizes the free variables automatically. But `E H` are also free. Let me write explicit parameters for clarity:

```lean
/-- A one-parameter family of Riemannian metrics on `M`. -/
abbrev MetricFamily (I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H) (M : Type*) [TopologicalSpace M]
    [ChartedSpace H M] := ℝ → Bundle.RiemannianMetric (fun x : M => TangentSpace I x)
```
Hmm, the typeclass `[(b : M) → TopologicalSpace (TangentSpace I b)]` etc. for `RiemannianMetric` are provided by the tangent bundle instances (`TangentBundle` gives `TopologicalSpace`, `AddCommGroup`, `Module` on fibers). Should be fine.

Then:
```lean
/-- The Ricci tensor at a point, as a family of bilinear forms on the tangent space. -/
abbrev RicciTensor (I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H) (M : Type*) [TopologicalSpace M]
    [ChartedSpace H M] := (x : M) → TangentSpace I x →L[ℝ] TangentSpace I x →L[ℝ] ℝ

abbrev RicciFamily (I M) := ℝ → RicciTensor I M
```

Then `HasMetricTimeDerivative`:
```lean
/-- `HasMetricTimeDerivative g dg t` means that at time `t` the scalar function
`s ↦ g s (v,w)` has derivative `dg v w`, for every point `x` and tangent vectors `v w`. -/
def HasMetricTimeDerivative (g : MetricFamily I M)
    (dg : (x : M) → TangentSpace I x →L[ℝ] TangentSpace I x →L[ℝ] ℝ) (t : ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (x : M) (v w : TangentSpace I x),
    HasDerivAt (fun s : ℝ => (g s).inner x v w) (dg x v w) t
```
Note: `(g s).inner x v w`: `g s : RiemannianMetric (fun x => TangentSpace I x)`, `.inner : (b : M) → ...`. Good.

Then:
```lean
/-- A candidate Ricci flow: data plus explicit hypotheses. -/
structure MetricFlowData (I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H) (M : Type*) [TopologicalSpace M]
    [ChartedSpace H M] where
  timeDomain : Set ℝ
  zero_mem : 0 ∈ timeDomain
  timeDomain_ordConnected : OrdConnected timeDomain
  metric : MetricFamily I M
  metric_time_smooth : ∀ (x : M) (v w : TangentSpace I x),
    ContDiff ℝ ⊤ (fun s : ℝ => (metric s).inner x v w)
  ricci : RicciFamily I M
  ricci_symm : ∀ (t : ℝ) (x : M) (v w : TangentSpace I x),
    ricci t x v w = ricci t x w v
  ricciFlow_equation : ∀ t ∈ timeDomain,
    HasMetricTimeDerivative metric (fun x _ v w => -2 * ricci t x v w) t
```
