### 2. Volume form

```lean
/-- The Gram matrix of the metric `g` at `x` in the basis `b` of the tangent space. -/
def gramMatrix {n : ℕ} (g : Bundle.RiemannianMetric (fun x : M => TangentSpace I x))
    (x : M) (b : Basis (Fin n) ℝ (TangentSpace I x)) : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ :=
  fun i j => g.inner x (b i) (b j)
```
Wait: is `TangentSpace I x` a module over ℝ? Yes, `TangentBundle` gives `Module ℝ`. `Basis (Fin n) ℝ (TangentSpace I x)` requires `[AddCommGroup] [Module ℝ]`, available. Also `[DecidableEq (Fin n)] [Fintype (Fin n)]` for `Matrix.det` — inferred.

```lean
/-- The Riemannian volume density at `x` in the frame `b`: the square root of the determinant of
the Gram matrix (the classical `√det g` coefficient). -/
def riemannianVolumeDensity {n : ℕ} (g : Bundle.RiemannianMetric (fun x : M => TangentSpace I x))
    (x : M) (b : Basis (Fin n) ℝ (TangentSpace I x)) : ℝ :=
  Real.sqrt (Matrix.det (gramMatrix g x b))
```
`Matrix.det` needs `CommRing ℝ` and instances; `gramMatrix` returns `Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ`. Good.

